"""
Generates intels-fr-ia.json: 100 intels (PUT /intel) in French on artificial intelligence, ten on each theme (models,
companies, regulation, security, research, hardware, people, uses, society, techniques). Each intel is a rule
"if … then …": the included entities with their weights, the excluded ones, the trigger level, fuzzy or not and the
instructions; then the places, times, related entities and questions; and its tags, events and signals. The ids are
stable (fr-ia-<slug of the title>): sending the file again overwrites the same documents.

Line format, fields separated by ' | ' ('-' for an empty field):
title | included (Name=weight, …) | excluded (Name, …) | level | fuzzy (0/1) | instructions |
locations (;) | times (;) | related entities (;) | questions (;) | tags | events | signals

Usage: python make_intels_fr_ia.py [--send]  (writes the JSON next to this script; --send also PUTs it to the server)
"""
